claim.claim-text:
a trolley (2) having a top side and a bottom side spaced from the top side, the trolley being horizontally movable in a substantially horizontal first direction (Y);
a platform (3) positioned on the top side of the trolley and comprising a first end (4), a second end (5) spaced from the first end, and a top surface (6) that extends in a substantially horizontal second direction (X) perpendicular to the first direction (Y) between the first and second ends, the top surface is configured to support the battery block thereon;
a lift mechanism (7) disposed between the trolley and the platform, the lift mechanism is configured to move the platform relative to the trolley in a substantially vertical third direction (Z) perpendicular to both the first and the second direction; and
a battery block moving mechanism (8) coupled to the platform and configured to move the battery block alongside the top surface (6) of the platform (2) in the second direction (X) so as to transfer the battery block from the top surface of the platform or to transfer the battery block to the top surface of the platform.

a battery block (23);
at least one rack (24) having a plurality of shelves (25), each shelf of the plurality of shelves being configured to receive and mechanically support the battery block, wherein the trolley moving mechanism of each of the at least one subsystem is adapted to move the trolley along the at least one rack, each shelf of the plurality of shelves being open toward the at least one rail in the first direction and the battery block moving mechanism (8) of each of the at least one subsystem is adapted to transfer the battery block from the top surface of the platform to a shelf of the plurality of shelves and from the shelf of the plurality of shelves to the top surface of the platform; and
at least one charging unit (26) each adapted to charge and communicate with the one battery block when the one battery block is received within one of the plurality of shelves (25).

a ramp (29) on which an electric vehicle can advance to the location of battery exchange in the second direction (X); and
a vehicle lane (30) under which the at least one subsystem moves in the first direction (Y);
wherein the vehicle lane has an opening (31), the opening being adapted to give free passage to the battery block when the battery block is lifted in the third direction (Z) by the lift mechanism of the at least one subsystem.
